\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces A real bug from Bugs4Q~\cite  {zhao2023bugs4q}, posted on Stack Overflow. (a)~The program meant to prepare $(\lvert 01\rangle +\lvert 10\rangle )/\sqrt  {2}$, and line~6 should apply $X$. (b)~The buggy outcomes are uniform over all four bit strings, yet each qubit alone looks as intended. (c)~Asked which lines determine $q_0$, the classical PDG keeps line~5 alone and misses the faulty line~6; the wire rule keeps lines~5 to~7. Outcomes, slices and dependences are computed by the study's code.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:motivating}{{1}{2}{}{figure.1}{}}
