\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Dependence graphs of two Qiskit programs. Nodes are operations, labelled with the source line that created them; edges are the dependences of the wire rule. (a,\,b)~Teleportation needs control dependence. The corrections on $q_2$ depend on the measurements through the green edges, which def-use ignores. (c,\,d)~A hardware-efficient VQE ansatz needs quantum dependence. The blue edges, where a CNOT changes its control, are missing from the classical PDG, whose slice of $q_0$ (bold) stops at $q_0$'s own rotations. Entanglement closure adds two rotations of $q_2$ that are not dependences (orange). $F$ is the criterion's fidelity at $\lvert 0\dots  0\rangle $. Graphs, slices and fidelities are computed by the study's code from the programs shown.}}{3}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dependence}{{2}{3}{}{figure.2}{}}
